# fifo_op_display_nub: The display opcodes' framing past the port lookup, with a shared state page set on port 0 (opcode 1) and no host display attached. Only the stamp's class is locked here, not the shared page (the display scenarios lock that). DisplaySetProperties walks its property records: a record cut short, a word count whose byte count overflows u32, values cut short, and an unknown property each end the walk, and the command signals anyway; a full colour matrix (property 0, 12 words) and an empty list signal too. Kernel-only commands name task 1 and fault; ICC profile lengths over the mapped length signal anyway.
